From f88e4fd35ab4d16767d8027878d9114c610876eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:41:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugins): task read API and run context for agent hooks

Plugins reacting to task.completed could learn that a run finished but never
what happened in it, and agent-trigger tools could not tell which run called
them. This adds the missing read slice to the Plugin Action API:

- GET /v1/tasks/{task_id}: the run (kind, links, attempt, status) and the
  input that started it (chat message, trigger comment, quick-create prompt,
  delegation handoff), each withheld unless its own read scope is granted.
- GET /v1/tasks/{task_id}/messages: the transcript, cursor-paginated, with
  long fields cut at 32 KiB.
- New scope chats:read: a chat run's input and transcript are a private
  conversation, so tasks:read alone never reveals them.
- Agent-trigger hook bodies carry task_id and issue_id of the calling run,
  taken from the claimed task row. The callback grant is narrowed to that run
  for task reads only; issue reads stay as wide as before.
- Task events narrow the callback grant to the run they report on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q7ExVGHb5smYmyoJ2CzYyd
